{
  "category": "Angler Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "It shoots positive and negative electricity between the tips of its two antennae and zaps its enemies.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "On the dark ocean floor, its only means of communi cation is its constantly flashing lights.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its antennae, which evolved from a fin, have both po sitive and negative charges flowing through them.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "CHINCHOU lets loose positive and negative electrical charges from its two antennas to make its prey faint. This POKéMON flashes its electric lights to exchange signals with others.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "CHINCHOU’s two antennas are filled with cells that generate strong electricity. This POKéMON’s cells create so much electrical power, it even makes itself tingle slightly.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it senses danger, it discharges positive and negative electricity from its two antennae. It lives in depths beyond sunlight’s reach.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "On the dark ocean floor, its only means of communication is its constantly flashing lights.",
